      <marc:subfield code="a">One common issue faced by today’s young people is their struggle to accept reality while also being unable to let go, leading to inner conflict and anxiety—a state of self-inflicted mental exhaustion, which is the central theme of this book. Drawing from both personal experience and real-life counseling cases, the author explores the nature of this internal struggle and offers practical, actionable strategies to help readers break free from their psychological dilemmas. The goal is to support young people in escaping the cycle of mental burnout and finding a healthier, more balanced mindset</marc:subfield>
